1
00:00:02,303 --> 00:00:05,273
♪ In the
not-too-distant future ♪

2
00:00:05,307 --> 00:00:08,543
♪ Way down in Deep 13 ♪

3
00:00:08,577 --> 00:00:11,747
♪ Dr. Forrester and TV's Frank ♪

4
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:14,915
♪ Were hatching an evil scheme ♪

5
00:00:14,948 --> 00:00:17,818
♪ They hired a temp
by the name of Mike ♪

6
00:00:17,852 --> 00:00:20,922
♪ Just a regular Joe
they didn't like ♪

7
00:00:20,955 --> 00:00:23,892
♪ Their experiment
needed a good test case ♪

8
00:00:23,925 --> 00:00:25,460
♪ So they conked
him on the noggin ♪

9
00:00:25,493 --> 00:00:27,862
♪ And they shot him into space ♪

10
00:00:27,895 --> 00:00:29,497
- [Mike] Let me go!

11
00:00:30,665 --> 00:00:33,602
♪ We'll send them
cheesy movies ♪

12
00:00:33,635 --> 00:00:36,703
♪ The worst we can
find (la la la) ♪

13
00:00:36,738 --> 00:00:39,573
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:39,607 --> 00:00:42,910
♪ And we'll monitor
his mind (la la la) ♪

15
00:00:42,943 --> 00:00:45,780
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

16
00:00:45,813 --> 00:00:49,217
♪ Where the movies begin
or end (la la la) ♪

17
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:51,853
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity ♪

18
00:00:51,887 --> 00:00:56,858
♪ With the help of
his robot friends ♪

19
00:00:57,658 --> 00:00:58,727
♪ Robot roll call ♪

20
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,128
♪ Cambot ♪

21
00:01:00,162 --> 00:01:01,462
♪ Gypsy ♪

22
00:01:01,495 --> 00:01:03,263
♪ Tom Servo ♪

23
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:04,765
♪ Crow ♪

24
00:01:04,798 --> 00:01:07,835
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

25
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:11,005
♪ And other science
facts (la la la) ♪

26
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:13,775
♪ Just repeat to yourself
it's just a show ♪

27
00:01:13,808 --> 00:01:16,878
♪ I should really just relax ♪

28
00:01:16,912 --> 00:01:21,148
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

29
00:01:26,553 --> 00:01:28,723
(beeping)

30
00:01:35,062 --> 00:01:36,663
(laughing)

31
00:01:36,697 --> 00:01:38,098
- Hi, everyone, welcome
to the Satellite of Love,

32
00:01:38,132 --> 00:01:39,967
where Tom and Crow
have planned something

33
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,870
which is apparently lovely.

34
00:01:41,903 --> 00:01:44,938
- Oh, and darling,
and just so lovely.

35
00:01:44,972 --> 00:01:45,773
- That's right.

36
00:01:45,807 --> 00:01:47,375
Oh, Gypsy!

37
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:49,410
- We're giving you a shower!

38
00:01:49,443 --> 00:01:50,378
- Huh?

39
00:01:50,412 --> 00:01:51,378
- Oh, look, she's surprised.

40
00:01:51,412 --> 00:01:52,880
Now isn't that just darling?

41
00:01:52,913 --> 00:01:55,350
- Well, I'm not getting
married, and, am I pregnant?

42
00:01:55,383 --> 00:01:58,085
- Oh, Gypsy, every
woman gets a shower,

43
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,020
and it's just so lovely!

44
00:02:00,053 --> 00:02:01,857
- Well, I'm pretty
sure I'm a woman.

45
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:04,525
- Open that one first,
Mike, it's from me.

46
00:02:04,558 --> 00:02:06,227
Doesn't she look lovely?

47
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,895
- It's pinking shears!

48
00:02:07,928 --> 00:02:09,797
- Oh, thank you!

49
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,333
How very thoughtful, and lovely!

50
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,702
- Oh, those are
just darling, Crow!

51
00:02:13,735 --> 00:02:15,703
Okay, this one's from me.

52
00:02:15,737 --> 00:02:17,272
- And it is pinking shears!

53
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:19,407
(all gasping)

54
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,908
- Oh, just like mine!

55
00:02:20,942 --> 00:02:22,277
How darling and lovely!

56
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:23,778
- Well, yeah, Gypsy,
I saw that Crow

57
00:02:23,812 --> 00:02:25,880
got you the same thing,
and that gave me the idea!

58
00:02:25,913 --> 00:02:27,315
(laughing)

59
00:02:27,348 --> 00:02:30,150
- Okay, this one is from Cambot,
and it is pinking shears!

60
00:02:30,185 --> 00:02:32,187
- Oh, I can get pinking!

61
00:02:34,322 --> 00:02:37,058
- Okay, now Tom and Crow
went in on one more for ya.

62
00:02:37,092 --> 00:02:38,292
- Oh, let me guess,
let me guess.

63
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:39,127
Pinking shears?

64
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,562
- Nope.

65
00:02:40,595 --> 00:02:42,430
Well, I guess it
is, pinking shears.

66
00:02:42,463 --> 00:02:44,032
- Darling and lovely.

67
00:02:44,065 --> 00:02:46,067
- Well, Tom saw them,
and I had to agree.

68
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,870
Just lovely and
darling, aren't they?

69
00:02:48,903 --> 00:02:51,438
(quirky music)

70
00:02:55,543 --> 00:02:57,778
- Well, this has been so nice.

71
00:02:57,812 --> 00:03:00,648
Thank you all so
much, I, uh, well,

72
00:03:00,682 --> 00:03:02,283
thanks, and everything.

73
00:03:02,317 --> 00:03:04,818
- It was so much fun, Gypsy!

74
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:06,888
You got so much great stuff.

75
00:03:06,922 --> 00:03:08,388
- Didn't she?

76
00:03:08,422 --> 00:03:09,890
- I really hope you like
the pinking shears, Gypsy.

77
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:12,827
I saw those in a catalog
and I just thought Gypsy.

78
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,128
- Oh, Tom, let me wrap up some
of that chicken salad for ya.

79
00:03:15,162 --> 00:03:16,263
- Don't you dare, no no.

80
00:03:16,297 --> 00:03:17,198
I'll explode.

81
00:03:17,232 --> 00:03:18,867
- Girls, the mads are calling.

82
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,335
- [Tom and Crow] Lovely!

83
00:03:21,368 --> 00:03:24,138
- Oh, sorry, didn't
know you had company.

84
00:03:24,172 --> 00:03:28,008
Say, Mike, you haven't seen
Frank around anywhere, have you?

85
00:03:28,042 --> 00:03:30,545
I've looked everywhere,
he didn't leave a note.

86
00:03:30,578 --> 00:03:32,580
The car keys are still here.

87
00:03:32,613 --> 00:03:34,548
He didn't mention
anything to you, did he?

88
00:03:34,582 --> 00:03:36,117
- No, nothing at all.

89
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,785
Did you try all
the Baskin Robbins?

90
00:03:37,818 --> 00:03:39,253
- Did you try
comic book college?

91
00:03:39,287 --> 00:03:40,755
- Did you try all
the emergency rooms?

92
00:03:40,788 --> 00:03:42,023
They all know him there.

93
00:03:42,057 --> 00:03:42,890
- Yeah.

94
00:03:44,492 --> 00:03:48,663
- In the Line of Fire,
Speed, Blown Away.

95
00:03:48,697 --> 00:03:49,930
Nelson, look!

96
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:51,465
I was just tidying
up in Frank's room

97
00:03:51,498 --> 00:03:55,135
and I found these ticket
stubs in Frank's pants pocket.

98
00:03:55,168 --> 00:03:56,537
Now I really am worried.

99
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,372
You know how easily
influenced Frank is

100
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:00,107
by the moving picture.

101
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,642
- Well, I wouldn't
worry about it, Dr. F.

102
00:04:01,675 --> 00:04:03,277
I'm sure he's not serious.

103
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,778
Oh, hey, check it out, Gypsy,

104
00:04:04,812 --> 00:04:06,913
there's another gift here
for you, isn't that lovely?

105
00:04:06,948 --> 00:04:08,215
- It's from Frank!

106
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,150
Listen to this.

107
00:04:09,183 --> 00:04:11,452
"Dear Gypsy, how are you?

108
00:04:11,485 --> 00:04:12,887
"I am fine.

109
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:16,890
"I am going to bomb the living
bejeesus out of Deep 13.

110
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:19,060
"Well, it looks like
I'm out of room.

111
00:04:19,093 --> 00:04:21,228
"Best wishes, Frank."

112
00:04:21,262 --> 00:04:22,997
Oh my god, Mike, Tom, Crow!

113
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:24,898
We've gotta stop him!

114
00:04:24,932 --> 00:04:27,735
Oh, "PS, hope you like
the pinking shears."

115
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:29,237
Oh, how very thoughtful.

116
00:04:29,270 --> 00:04:30,972
- Well, I wouldn't
worry about it,

117
00:04:31,005 --> 00:04:32,440
I'm sure Frank's not serious.

118
00:04:32,473 --> 00:04:33,642
- He sure is, Mike.

119
00:04:33,675 --> 00:04:35,108
Those are definitely
pinking shears.

120
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:37,245
- Not about the pinking,
I'm talking about the bomb.

121
00:04:37,278 --> 00:04:38,478
Hey, Dr. F, I think
you should know

122
00:04:38,512 --> 00:04:40,615
about this bomb
threat from Frank.

123
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:43,150
- I knew it, I knew it!

124
00:04:43,183 --> 00:04:45,420
Just look at what I
found in Frank's closet

125
00:04:45,453 --> 00:04:47,388
behind his Jane West doll.

126
00:04:47,422 --> 00:04:48,757
Dynamite.

127
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:50,558
Not that I was snooping.

128
00:04:50,592 --> 00:04:51,792
But if I didn't
snoop, I wouldn't know

129
00:04:51,825 --> 00:04:54,162
what was going on
in Frank's life.

130
00:04:54,195 --> 00:04:57,565
All right, Mickey, I've got
it taken care of down here.

131
00:04:57,598 --> 00:05:01,802
Why don't you take in Ed
Wood's The Sinister Urge,

132
00:05:01,835 --> 00:05:05,305
with a short about
personal hygiene.

133
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,775
Watch and learn, stink bombs.

134
00:05:09,743 --> 00:05:11,445
- This one's got good heft.

135
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:13,647
Well, anyway, call us if you
need us, Clay, all right?

136
00:05:13,682 --> 00:05:15,215
- Well, Gypsy, I think Frank
would be really understanding

137
00:05:15,248 --> 00:05:17,918
if you return his pinking
shears and got something else.

138
00:05:17,952 --> 00:05:19,153
(alarm sounding)
(shouting)

139
00:05:19,187 --> 00:05:21,922
- Oh, great, we've
got movie sign!

140
00:05:35,437 --> 00:05:37,138
(lighthearted orchestral music)

141
00:05:37,172 --> 00:05:38,773
(humming)

142
00:05:38,807 --> 00:05:41,375
- [Mike] Wendell Yeo, the
cleanest man in Boston.

143
00:05:41,408 --> 00:05:44,645
- What, were these
sold door to door?

144
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:47,013
- [Tom] Join us, join us.

145
00:05:47,048 --> 00:05:48,582
- In the eighth grade.

146
00:05:48,615 --> 00:05:51,752
They want to choose a boy
and a girl from this class

147
00:05:51,785 --> 00:05:53,587
to be in their assembly.

148
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,655
- [Tom] Who wants
to be sacrificed?

149
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:55,990
- All right, put
your hands down.

150
00:05:56,023 --> 00:05:57,725
They'll have to choose.

151
00:05:57,758 --> 00:06:00,127
- [Mike] The eighth-graders
cull the herd.

152
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,795
- [Narrator] Whomever
John and Arlene choose,

153
00:06:01,828 --> 00:06:03,430
you can be sure of one thing.

154
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:05,867
It won't be anyone who
isn't clean and neat.

155
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,735
- [Crow] They'll sniff everyone.

156
00:06:07,768 --> 00:06:09,270
- [Narrator] Looking clean
and neat is something

157
00:06:09,303 --> 00:06:11,838
everyone is expected to do,
and for a very good reason.

158
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,240
- [Tom] Here's the
shrooms, Billy.

159
00:06:13,273 --> 00:06:14,475
- [Narrator] It's
important to your health,

160
00:06:14,508 --> 00:06:17,043
and to the health
of those around you.

161
00:06:17,078 --> 00:06:19,213
Don may feel that he
looks neat enough.

162
00:06:19,247 --> 00:06:20,715
- But Don's wrong.

163
00:06:20,748 --> 00:06:22,750
- [Narrator] But let's go
back to the start of the day

164
00:06:22,783 --> 00:06:24,685
and see what we can do.

165
00:06:25,887 --> 00:06:28,222
There you are, Don, back
in bed this morning.

166
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:29,723
- Now, a giant cockroach.

167
00:06:29,757 --> 00:06:31,558
- [Narrator] First of all,
form the habit of getting up

168
00:06:31,592 --> 00:06:32,727
in plenty of time.

169
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,162
- [Tom] To sober up.

170
00:06:34,195 --> 00:06:35,697
- [Narrator] Keeping
clean and neat is a matter

171
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:38,332
of forming good habits and
letting them work for you.

172
00:06:38,365 --> 00:06:40,868
- [Mike] Oh man, what the
hell did I do last night?

173
00:06:40,902 --> 00:06:42,337
- [Narrator] Now, don't stall.

174
00:06:42,370 --> 00:06:44,105
If you lie in bed so long
that you have to rush,

175
00:06:44,138 --> 00:06:46,407
how can you expect
to be neat and clean?

176
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:49,177
- Lay off, you're
suffocating me!

177
00:06:50,512 --> 00:06:53,713
(humming "Psycho" theme)

178
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:55,215
- [Tom] Psycho.

179
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,183
- [Narrator] Or in winter,
when you're hot and sweaty,

180
00:06:56,217 --> 00:06:57,785
every other day will do.

181
00:06:57,818 --> 00:07:00,688
Make it a shower or a
tub, whichever you like,

182
00:07:00,722 --> 00:07:02,190
morning or night.

183
00:07:02,223 --> 00:07:04,758
It doesn't matter, just so
you keep yourself clean.

184
00:07:04,792 --> 00:07:06,593
- [Mike] Use a
Brillo pad and Comet.

185
00:07:06,627 --> 00:07:07,628
- [Narrator] Remember your ears.

186
00:07:07,662 --> 00:07:09,230
They need a soapy washcloth.

187
00:07:09,263 --> 00:07:13,133
- Kerosene and a match
gets rid of the ear mites.

188
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:14,535
- [Narrator] When
you wash your feet,

189
00:07:14,568 --> 00:07:15,803
be sure to get between your toes

190
00:07:15,837 --> 00:07:17,505
and the bottom of your feet.

191
00:07:17,538 --> 00:07:18,538
- [Tom] But you'll never
be able to scrub away

192
00:07:18,572 --> 00:07:20,508
the stain on your soul.

193
00:07:22,743 --> 00:07:23,845
- [Narrator] And keep a
fingernail brush handy

194
00:07:23,878 --> 00:07:25,112
for your nails.

195
00:07:25,145 --> 00:07:27,582
You're not clean if
your fingernails aren't.

196
00:07:27,615 --> 00:07:29,717
- [Mike] You are now officially
obsessive-compulsive.

197
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:31,118
- [Narrator] Then
rinse all the soap off.

198
00:07:31,152 --> 00:07:32,687
- [Tom] Rinse,
dammit, rinse, rinse!

199
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,922
- [Narrator] Learn to make
good habits work for you

200
00:07:33,955 --> 00:07:35,990
by following the same
order every time.

201
00:07:36,023 --> 00:07:39,793
- So clean yourself
in alphabetical order.

202
00:07:39,827 --> 00:07:42,830
- [Tom] Use pumice on
your tender nipple buds.

203
00:07:42,863 --> 00:07:44,065
- [Narrator] And
here's another habit.

204
00:07:44,098 --> 00:07:46,933
Wash your hair on the
same day each week.

205
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:50,203
Tuesday, Wednesday, Saturday,
whichever day you choose.

206
00:07:50,237 --> 00:07:52,740
- [Mike] Keep a
detailed log, though.

207
00:07:52,773 --> 00:07:54,775
- [Narrator] Use a
good shampoo or soap,

208
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:56,677
and rub in the lather
with your fingers,

209
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,145
not your fingernails.

210
00:07:58,178 --> 00:07:59,813
- [Mike] Here, let me help you.

211
00:07:59,847 --> 00:08:02,217
- [Narrator] Lather up twice,
with a rinse in between.

212
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:03,683
- Why couldn't they
have had Mamie Van Doren

213
00:08:03,717 --> 00:08:05,285
star in this thing?

214
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,188
- [Narrator] And after
the second lather,

215
00:08:08,222 --> 00:08:11,525
when your hair is perfectly
clean, rinse again.

216
00:08:11,558 --> 00:08:14,328
Keep rinsing til every
bit of soap is out.

217
00:08:14,362 --> 00:08:16,063
- [Tom] (imitating knocking)
You almost done in there?

218
00:08:16,097 --> 00:08:17,698
What are you doing?

219
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,968
(humming)

220
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:22,837
- [Narrator] There.

221
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:24,105
Feels good, doesn't it?

222
00:08:24,138 --> 00:08:25,640
- [Tom] No no no,
don't touch that.

223
00:08:25,673 --> 00:08:26,773
- [Narrator] Give yourself a
good rubdown with the towel

224
00:08:26,807 --> 00:08:29,177
until you're completely dry.

225
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:30,477
- [Mike] Please remain
seated until the shower

226
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,313
has come to a full
and complete stop.

227
00:08:32,347 --> 00:08:33,547
- [Narrator] Now, before
you brush your hair,

228
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,650
be sure your comb
and brush are clean.

229
00:08:35,683 --> 00:08:37,117
- He's becoming Howard Hughes!

230
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,752
- [Narrator] Wash them the
day you wash your hair.

231
00:08:38,785 --> 00:08:42,590
- [Tom] Have an extensive
filter system installed.

232
00:08:42,623 --> 00:08:45,192
- [Mike] Comb your
Darren Stevens haircut.

233
00:08:45,225 --> 00:08:46,027
- [Narrator] Your teeth--

234
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,428
- [Tom] Comb them too.

235
00:08:47,462 --> 00:08:49,763
- [Narrator] They're clean now.

236
00:08:49,797 --> 00:08:51,265
Brush them again
after breakfast,

237
00:08:51,298 --> 00:08:53,100
so they'll be clean
again til lunch.

238
00:08:53,133 --> 00:08:55,268
- Aha, aha, mad dog, aha!

239
00:08:55,302 --> 00:08:57,572
- [Narrator] Before
you leave the bathroom,

240
00:08:57,605 --> 00:08:58,805
- [Tom] Flush.

241
00:08:58,838 --> 00:09:00,642
- [Narrator] See that it
is neat and clean too.

242
00:09:00,675 --> 00:09:03,677
Towel and wash cloth
hung up to dry.

243
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:06,013
Cap back on the shampoo.

244
00:09:06,047 --> 00:09:07,748
- [Mike] Dun-dun-dun!

245
00:09:07,782 --> 00:09:10,183
- [Narrator] Bathtub clean.

246
00:09:10,217 --> 00:09:11,552
Basin clean.

247
00:09:11,585 --> 00:09:13,553
- Pick up all the
hairs with a tweezer.

248
00:09:13,587 --> 00:09:15,455
- [Narrator] Yes,
everything is put away.

249
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:17,325
- [Tom] Now have
the bathroom sealed.

250
00:09:17,358 --> 00:09:18,960
- [Narrator] Now your clothes.

251
00:09:18,993 --> 00:09:21,095
Your underwear should be
just as clean as you are.

252
00:09:21,128 --> 00:09:22,930
- [Mike] Hey, don't
say underwear.

253
00:09:22,963 --> 00:09:24,865
- [Narrator] Clean socks.

254
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:26,333
But look at those shoes.

255
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:28,668
- Uh-oh, Dad's vomit.

256
00:09:28,702 --> 00:09:31,705
- [Narrator] What you
need is the shoeshine kit.

257
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:33,240
- [Mike] There, now
wear this instead.

258
00:09:33,273 --> 00:09:35,575
- [Narrator] You can make one
like this yourself, you know.

259
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:38,178
- [Tom] But that's a
whole 'nother film.

260
00:09:38,212 --> 00:09:39,380
- [Narrator] That's
better, isn't it?

261
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,882
- [Mike] What the hell is that?

262
00:09:40,915 --> 00:09:42,317
- [Narrator] Be sure the
top is back on the polish.

263
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:45,152
- Does this kid have
a job interview?

264
00:09:45,185 --> 00:09:47,253
- [Narrator] Uh-oh, that's
no way to treat your clothes.

265
00:09:47,288 --> 00:09:49,290
- [Mike] But that's
how they treat me!

266
00:09:49,323 --> 00:09:51,025
- [Narrator] If they're
clean enough to wear again,

267
00:09:51,058 --> 00:09:52,025
hang them up.

268
00:09:52,058 --> 00:09:53,427
- Or just have your mom do it.

269
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:56,263
- [Narrator] Fold the
trousers neatly over a hanger.

270
00:09:56,297 --> 00:09:57,498
- [Tom] There, that's it.

271
00:09:57,532 --> 00:09:58,898
Work it now, there ya go.

272
00:09:58,932 --> 00:10:01,268
(chuckling)

273
00:10:02,703 --> 00:10:05,873
- [Mike] It's about three
in the afternoon by now.

274
00:10:05,907 --> 00:10:07,975
- [Narrator] Put the
shirts on hangers, too.

275
00:10:08,008 --> 00:10:11,045
Hang them up in your closet.

276
00:10:11,078 --> 00:10:13,313
Look at that closet!

277
00:10:13,347 --> 00:10:17,652
Before you do another thing,
get busy and straighten it out.

278
00:10:17,685 --> 00:10:18,918
- Ahh!

279
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:22,423
Shift into another time
dimension, if it helps.

280
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,993
- [Tom] Uh-oh, now your
hands are filthy again.

281
00:10:26,027 --> 00:10:27,428
- [Narrator] Hard
work, isn't it?

282
00:10:27,462 --> 00:10:29,930
But if you learn the
habit of keeping it neat,

283
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:32,198
you'll never have to go
through anything like this.

284
00:10:32,232 --> 00:10:34,168
- Now, time for bed!

285
00:10:34,202 --> 00:10:35,770
- [Narrator] Now
then, a clean shirt,

286
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:37,538
and you're ready to
take a look at yourself.

287
00:10:37,572 --> 00:10:40,040
- [Mike] You despise
what you see.

288
00:10:40,073 --> 00:10:41,008
- [Narrator] Hair combed.

289
00:10:41,042 --> 00:10:42,242
- [Tom] Ehhhh!

290
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,012
- [Narrator] Face, ears,
and neck all clean.

291
00:10:44,045 --> 00:10:45,612
- And hot-waxed.

292
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:47,147
- [Narrator] Cuffs buttoned.

293
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:47,982
Clean hands.

294
00:10:48,015 --> 00:10:49,350
- [Mike] It's stigmata!

295
00:10:49,383 --> 00:10:51,885
- [Tom] Oh, the things
those hands will do.

296
00:10:51,918 --> 00:10:53,953
- [Narrator] Shirt
buttoned and tucked in.

297
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:57,425
Belt through all the loops,
trousers buttoned or zipped.

298
00:10:57,458 --> 00:10:58,625
- [Mike] Or not.

299
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,695
- [Narrator] Socks
pulled up, shoes shined,

300
00:11:00,728 --> 00:11:02,195
and shoelaces tied.

301
00:11:02,228 --> 00:11:04,765
- Now to get pantsed and
dragged around the track.

302
00:11:04,798 --> 00:11:05,867
- [Narrator] Not bad.

303
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:06,833
Not bad at all.

304
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:08,368
- [Mike] Ew, he's got fangs!

305
00:11:08,402 --> 00:11:09,637
- [Tom] Ahhh!

306
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:10,872
- [Narrator] Quite
a bit better than

307
00:11:10,905 --> 00:11:11,905
the way you looked in
class this morning.

308
00:11:11,938 --> 00:11:13,173
- [Tom] I'll say.

309
00:11:13,207 --> 00:11:14,442
- You pig.

310
00:11:14,475 --> 00:11:15,910
- [Narrator] Now how
about you, Mildred?

311
00:11:15,943 --> 00:11:20,013
Let's see what habits will
help you keep neat and clean.

312
00:11:20,047 --> 00:11:22,450
- [Tom] Mother Teresa!

313
00:11:22,483 --> 00:11:23,917
- [Narrator] Girls
have to wash their hair

314
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:26,587
in the afternoon or evening,
so there's time to put it up.

315
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,355
Don't go to bed with wet hair.

316
00:11:28,388 --> 00:11:29,723
- Or a first date.

317
00:11:29,757 --> 00:11:31,125
- [Narrator] Putting up
your hair is something

318
00:11:31,158 --> 00:11:34,095
you have to learn, and
everyone does it differently.

319
00:11:34,128 --> 00:11:35,562
It depends on how you wear it.

320
00:11:35,595 --> 00:11:38,065
♪ Take the ribbon from my hair ♪

321
00:11:38,098 --> 00:11:40,968
You may still need to get
help from your mother on this.

322
00:11:41,002 --> 00:11:43,737
- She's getting ready for
her date with Jerry Seinfeld.

323
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:46,607
- [Narrator] This is a good
time to trim your fingernails.

324
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,875
Make a habit of doing it
the day you wash your hair.

325
00:11:48,908 --> 00:11:51,178
- [Tom] Every leap year.

326
00:11:51,212 --> 00:11:53,313
- [Narrator] Boys like to
use fingernail clippers,

327
00:11:53,347 --> 00:11:56,017
but girls can shape them
better with an emery board.

328
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:57,283
- [Mike] Are you supposed
to file open sores

329
00:11:57,317 --> 00:11:58,852
with an emery board?

330
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:00,087
- [Narrator] And see
that little sore place

331
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,755
where you pulled away the skin?

332
00:12:01,788 --> 00:12:03,490
Next time, ask your
mother to cut it,

333
00:12:03,523 --> 00:12:05,860
and you won't have a
sore place like that.

334
00:12:05,893 --> 00:12:09,263
- Or just amputate that finger.

335
00:12:09,297 --> 00:12:11,532
- [Tom] Wait a
minute, only nine?

336
00:12:11,565 --> 00:12:13,167
- [Narrator] Don't
forget your toenails.

337
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,102
After a bath is a
good time to cut them,

338
00:12:15,135 --> 00:12:16,703
because they're softer then.

339
00:12:16,737 --> 00:12:18,538
- [Mike] Yeah, he knows a
lot about women's toenails.

340
00:12:18,572 --> 00:12:19,773
- [Narrator] Cut
them straight across,

341
00:12:19,807 --> 00:12:21,342
and not rounded
like fingernails.

342
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:22,477
- Better yet, cut 'em pointy!

343
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:24,178
Get a pinking shear!

344
00:12:26,747 --> 00:12:28,182
(humming)

345
00:12:28,215 --> 00:12:31,085
- [Narrator] Oh, Mildred,
look at your clothes!

346
00:12:31,118 --> 00:12:32,687
Why, that's as bad as Don was.

347
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,853
- [Tom] Don Was, the producer?

348
00:12:33,887 --> 00:12:34,788
- [Narrator] Things
that are dirty

349
00:12:34,822 --> 00:12:36,023
should go into the laundry.

350
00:12:36,057 --> 00:12:37,692
Things that are clean
enough to wear again

351
00:12:37,725 --> 00:12:39,760
should be folded and put away.

352
00:12:39,793 --> 00:12:41,195
- [Tom] Really.

353
00:12:41,228 --> 00:12:41,995
- [Narrator] Make sure
there are no wrinkles in it

354
00:12:42,028 --> 00:12:43,030
when you fold it.

355
00:12:43,063 --> 00:12:44,398
- What about the fold?

356
00:12:44,432 --> 00:12:45,565
- [Narrator] And
that dresser drawer!

357
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,000
- [Mike] I've
rummaged through it.

358
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:49,237
- [Narrator] Better straighten
it out this very minute.

359
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:53,007
- [Tom] Why can't a
woman be more like a man?

360
00:12:54,242 --> 00:12:55,442
- [Mike] In the '50s,
people responded well

361
00:12:55,475 --> 00:12:58,845
to authoritative
disembodied voices.

362
00:12:58,878 --> 00:13:01,315
- Haha, the fun never stops
when you're clean and tidy!

363
00:13:01,348 --> 00:13:04,218
(laughing)

364
00:13:04,252 --> 00:13:06,853
(humming along to the music)

365
00:13:06,887 --> 00:13:08,088
- [Narrator] There.

366
00:13:08,122 --> 00:13:09,557
If you learn the habit
of keeping it neat,

367
00:13:09,590 --> 00:13:11,558
you'll never have to go
through anything like this.

368
00:13:11,592 --> 00:13:13,227
- [Tom] Should I be a
nurse or a housewife?

369
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,762
Hmmmm.

370
00:13:14,795 --> 00:13:16,430
- [Narrator] And now that the
room is neat and you're clean,

371
00:13:16,463 --> 00:13:18,332
isn't it nice to climb into bed?

372
00:13:18,365 --> 00:13:22,135
- [Mike] Unfortunately,
it's time for school.

373
00:13:23,503 --> 00:13:26,173
- [Tom] Goodnight, Neely O'Hara.

374
00:13:28,542 --> 00:13:30,343
- [Narrator] In the morning,
give yourself plenty of time.

375
00:13:30,377 --> 00:13:31,745
- Say, six hours.

376
00:13:31,778 --> 00:13:34,013
- [Narrator] Get a
brush, and be neat.

377
00:13:34,047 --> 00:13:35,415
Be sure your
underthings are clean.

378
00:13:35,448 --> 00:13:38,585
- [Mike] Don't say underthings!

379
00:13:38,618 --> 00:13:40,553
- [Tom] Well, are they?

380
00:13:43,223 --> 00:13:45,625
- [Narrator] Your shoes
should go on over clean socks.

381
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,460
And take a look at your shoes.

382
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:49,162
Are they as neat
as they should be?

383
00:13:49,197 --> 00:13:50,865
- You know, the narrator should
get back over to Johnny's.

384
00:13:50,898 --> 00:13:53,233
He's probably a mess by now.

385
00:13:54,935 --> 00:13:56,037
- [Narrator] Before
you put on your dress.

386
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:57,337
- [Mike] Caress!

387
00:13:57,370 --> 00:13:58,838
- [Narrator] It's a good
idea to brush your hair.

388
00:13:58,872 --> 00:14:00,540
Be sure you've
washed your brush.

389
00:14:00,573 --> 00:14:03,710
Don't put a dirty
brush on clean hair.

390
00:14:03,743 --> 00:14:08,048
Brush and brush and brush,
at least 100 strokes.

391
00:14:08,082 --> 00:14:09,983
- [Mike] Just keep
brushing and brushing and

392
00:14:10,017 --> 00:14:13,253
saying the name of
our Lord and Savior.

393
00:14:17,323 --> 00:14:19,560
- [Narrator] There,
look how it shines.

394
00:14:19,593 --> 00:14:22,195
You did get all the soap
out last night, didn't you?

395
00:14:22,228 --> 00:14:24,265
- [Tom] Tail n'
Mane really works.

396
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:25,132
- [Narrator] And now.

397
00:14:25,165 --> 00:14:26,067
- [Mike] The weather.

398
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:27,533
- [Narrator] What dress to wear.

399
00:14:27,568 --> 00:14:29,737
Your dress has to be
suited to the occasion.

400
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:31,238
- Oh, that one's just fine.

401
00:14:31,272 --> 00:14:32,105
Let's go.

402
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:36,877
- [Mike] What is my
purpose in this world?

403
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:39,045
- [Narrator] No, that's
a lovely party dress,

404
00:14:39,078 --> 00:14:41,048
but it's too dressy for school.

405
00:14:41,082 --> 00:14:45,752
- [Tom] Don't go tramping
yourself up like that.

406
00:14:45,785 --> 00:14:47,187
- [Narrator] There,
that's more like it.

407
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,655
- Oh, I love that on you!

408
00:14:48,688 --> 00:14:50,723
- [Narrator] But would
another color look better?

409
00:14:50,757 --> 00:14:53,093
As you watch colors, you'll
learn what combinations

410
00:14:53,127 --> 00:14:54,495
look best on you.

411
00:14:54,528 --> 00:14:56,563
- [Mike] Learn to
mistrust your own taste.

412
00:14:56,597 --> 00:14:58,532
- [Narrator] And
now, how do you look?

413
00:14:58,565 --> 00:14:59,933
- [Tom] Kinda parochial.

414
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:01,268
- [Narrator] You can see
what a big difference

415
00:15:01,302 --> 00:15:03,570
a little extra care can
make in your appearance.

416
00:15:03,603 --> 00:15:04,738
- [Mike] Who am I trying to kid?

417
00:15:04,772 --> 00:15:08,542
I've hit the glass
ceiling of fifth grade.

418
00:15:08,575 --> 00:15:09,477
- [Narrator] Good
appearance helps you

419
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:10,945
get along with others.

420
00:15:10,978 --> 00:15:12,980
- Remember, people like you
better if you're pretty.

421
00:15:13,013 --> 00:15:14,213
- [Tom] Conform!

422
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:15,315
- [Narrator] Keeping
clean and neat is,

423
00:15:15,348 --> 00:15:17,083
and for our community.

424
00:15:17,117 --> 00:15:18,552
- And to fight Communism.

425
00:15:18,585 --> 00:15:19,787
- [Narrator] It's simply a
matter of learning good habits

426
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,857
and letting them work for you.

427
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:24,257
Don't you think you can do it?

428
00:15:24,292 --> 00:15:26,527
- Let's get clean together.

429
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,695
- [Mike] Can I carry your
soap home from school?

430
00:15:28,728 --> 00:15:32,967
- [Tom] And now back to the
drudgery that is your life.

431
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,802
- Thank you, thank
you, thank you.

432
00:15:34,835 --> 00:15:37,437
(quirky music)

433
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:43,377
- [Mike] Ah!

434
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:46,013
- [Tom] The scantily-clad prey.

435
00:15:47,347 --> 00:15:48,515
- The Maidenform woman!

436
00:15:48,548 --> 00:15:50,250
You'll never know
where she'll turn up.

437
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:52,485
(laughing)

438
00:15:52,518 --> 00:15:53,887
- [Mike] And Rosie
Ruiz takes the lead

439
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,822
in the Boston Marathon.

440
00:15:55,855 --> 00:15:57,858
- [Tom] Hey, she's trying
to give someone the slip.

441
00:15:57,892 --> 00:16:00,995
(laughing)
- [Mike] Oh, I love this game.

442
00:16:01,028 --> 00:16:02,462
The sinister urge
is a silly urge.

443
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:06,133
- [Tom] The sinister
urge is a stupid urge.

444
00:16:06,167 --> 00:16:11,172
- Looks like a pump, feels
like a pump, lemme tell ya.

445
00:16:12,605 --> 00:16:15,608
- [Mike] She must be one of
Senator Packwood's aides.

446
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:17,110
- [Tom] And she's down to
the pits for a new slip,

447
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:21,648
she's got the Junior Johnson
pit crew helping her out.

448
00:16:22,950 --> 00:16:24,452
- Oh, help me, help me!

449
00:16:24,485 --> 00:16:25,818
Oh, what a lovely spot.

450
00:16:25,852 --> 00:16:26,687
Help!

451
00:16:28,122 --> 00:16:31,792
- [Mike] She's here for
the Lutheran picnic.

452
00:16:32,893 --> 00:16:34,395
- [Tom] (gasping) Courtney Love!

453
00:16:34,428 --> 00:16:37,597
- This fall on ABC,
Get Courtney Love.

454
00:16:40,267 --> 00:16:41,968
- [Mike] Quickly,
into the TARDIS.

455
00:16:42,002 --> 00:16:43,270
- The what?

456
00:16:43,303 --> 00:16:44,538
- [Mike] TARDIS?

457
00:16:44,572 --> 00:16:47,373
- [Tom] You're not
dealing with AT&T.

458
00:16:48,808 --> 00:16:49,743
- Operator!

459
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:51,812
Operator!

460
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:53,113
- [Tom] Get me Sylvia's mother!

461
00:16:53,147 --> 00:16:54,515
- Operator!

462
00:16:54,548 --> 00:16:56,950
Operator!
(phone ringing)

463
00:16:56,983 --> 00:17:00,620
- [Tom] Richard
Diamond, Operator.

464
00:17:00,653 --> 00:17:01,455
- Yeeeees?

465
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:04,758
- [Tom] No, Jesus
isn't on the line.

466
00:17:04,792 --> 00:17:06,327
- Where?

467
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,962
Yeah, yeah, hold on a minute.

468
00:17:08,995 --> 00:17:09,930
Kline!

469
00:17:09,963 --> 00:17:11,532
- Kline!
- Kline!

470
00:17:11,565 --> 00:17:12,867
(cheering)

471
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,000
- That's my favorite character!

472
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,602
- Get all this information.

473
00:17:15,635 --> 00:17:17,103
- Yes, sir.

474
00:17:17,137 --> 00:17:20,540
- Then get a squad
car ready right away.

475
00:17:20,573 --> 00:17:22,575
(laughing)

476
00:17:22,608 --> 00:17:23,610
- [Mike] You don't direct Kline,

477
00:17:23,643 --> 00:17:25,578
you just get out of the way.

478
00:17:25,612 --> 00:17:28,048
- You just stay right where
you are. We're on our way.

479
00:17:28,082 --> 00:17:31,752
- Where are you, by
the way, damn, oh.

480
00:17:31,785 --> 00:17:35,522
- [Tom] Great, a murder
on a Friday afternoon.

481
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:37,123
- Randy, we're going out.

482
00:17:37,157 --> 00:17:41,095
- [Mike] Wow, he's
got a huge precinct.

483
00:17:41,128 --> 00:17:46,032
- Let's see here, spectacles,
testicles, wallet, and watch.

484
00:17:48,935 --> 00:17:51,003
- What's up, Matt?
- [Tom] I was waiting for you!

485
00:17:51,037 --> 00:17:52,205
- Found another girl.

486
00:17:52,238 --> 00:17:53,040
- Where?

487
00:17:53,073 --> 00:17:54,508
- Same place, the park.

488
00:17:54,542 --> 00:17:55,442
- Oh no.

489
00:17:55,475 --> 00:17:56,210
- [Mike] Another girl, huh?

490
00:17:56,243 --> 00:17:57,043
Is she pretty?

491
00:17:57,077 --> 00:17:57,878
Does she have a friend?

